  "body": "**Original comment by Sebastien Guyader (Bitbucket: [Sebastien Guyader](https://bitbucket.org/Sebastien Guyader), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nIt’s much better now. However, it still leaves some faint artifacts. If I switch to mono demosaicing and then back to xtrans demosaicing, those artifacts disappear, and I’d say the image is even a bit sharper on some images.\n\nHere’s a screenshot from the [pixls.us](http://pixls.us) forum, showing the artifacts zoomed in. Left is new ART, right is also new ART but after switch back and forth between mono and xtrans demosaicing.\n\n![](https://bitbucket.org/repo/9pArXyE/images/1300201829-2020-05-15_09-37.jpg)\nBut it’s heavy pixel peeping, and as it is now I think it is good, and already an improvement.\n",
